Description: drop PHP Build-Depends for nocheck-gated tests
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-17
Bug-Athena: libsoup2.4 declares php / libapache2-mod-php as build-deps
 gated <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>.  When our build container runs
 dpkg-buildpackage with DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc,nocheck via env,
 the profile filtering isn't being honored consistently by the
 internal dep check — fails with
 "Unmet build dependencies: php (<< 2:9) php (>= 2:7)".
 .
 These deps are ONLY for the HTTP testsuite (libsoup2.4 historically
 ran apache+PHP to test HTTP client behaviour against a live server).
 Our build profile already disables tests (nocheck), so the deps
 are dead weight anyway.  Drop them entirely — they're never
 satisfied in our pool and never needed.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -9,8 +9,6 @@ Build-Depends: apache2 (>= 2.4) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
                dh-sequence-gnome,
                glib-networking (>= 2.32.0),
                gtk-doc-tools,
-               libapache2-mod-php (<< 2:9) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
-               libapache2-mod-php (>= 2:7) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
                libbrotli-dev,
                libgirepository1.0-dev (>= 0.9.5),
                libglib2.0-dev (>= 2.58),
@@ -22,9 +20,6 @@ Build-Depends: apache2 (>= 2.4) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
                libsqlite3-dev,
                libxml2-dev,
                meson (>= 0.48),
-               php (<< 2:9) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
-               php (>= 2:7) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
-               php-xmlrpc <!nocheck> <!noinsttest> | php (>= 2:8.1+85+really8) <!nocheck> <!noinsttest>,
                python3,
                valac
 Build-Depends-Indep: libglib2.0-doc
